From e6c6f19cc2be6a8effd83618adab143fb2519597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshkamdar67 <harshkamdar67@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:13:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] inkling2: tagged mask from the CPU, attention over the
 cells of the batch's sequences only

The tagged mask is filled on the CPU, which knows the few cells near the batch: no distance of every cell to every
token and no tag pass per layer (118 ms -> 15 ms per 512 tokens at 128K). Sequences that share a cache keep to a
region each, and the full-attention layers read the range of the batch's sequences, not the whole pool.
